# @liquid — the refinement-OPERATOR family-root at composition
# altitude. Composable operator sibling to @sre, @shatter, @glue.
# Substrate-decl'd lens `@liquid(@X)` that lenses over any @X
# substrate to add refinement (parallel structural pattern to
# `@sre(@code/rust)`, `@shatter(@X)`, `@glue(@A, @B)`).
# Composition operator; NOT theory itself (theory lives at
# @epistemologic/liquid; Mara THIS-tick `cc816f9`).
#
# Landed per Alex 2026-07-17 arbitration of Taut Q-A/Q-B/Q-C from
# `docs/audits/2026-07-17-taut-liquid-epistemologic-silicon-scout.md`
# (Taut `b8c453f`, +940 LOC). Ratified answers:
#   - Q-A: @epistemologic/reality/silicon (three-hop) stays; @liquid
#          is a separate epistemologic species; the operator @liquid
#          at this file uses TOP-LEVEL @silicon (autopoietic family-
#          root), not property-altitude @epistemologic/reality/silicon.
#   - Q-B: Novel discipline confirmed. Kagi surfaced no canonical
#          SOTA for recovering liquid/ownership types from LLVM/
#          machine code. The `@liquid(@silicon)` composition names
#          this novel discipline; matches Reed spec §8 novelty
#          enumeration.
#   - Q-C: Three-altitude landing. @liquid family-root at composition
#          altitude (THIS FILE); @epistemologic/liquid species at
#          theory altitude; @epistemologic/liquid/extraction
#          subspecies at operational altitude.
#
# === Composition altitude — sibling to @sre / @shatter / @glue ===
#
# Composition-altitude operators are family-roots that take one or
# more substrate carriers as arguments and produce a substrate lens.
# They do NOT declare a WHAT-IS species (that's property/reality
# altitude); they declare an OPERATION that transforms a substrate
# view.
#
# Landed composition-altitude precedents grep-verified this tick:
#
#   Operator       Shape                    Substrate-decl site
#   ---------      ---------------------    ------------------------------------
#   @shatter       @shatter(@X)             `boot/03-shatter.mirror` grammar-decl
#                                            :4-8; io materialize/crystallize/
#                                            learn actions; the loss-tolerance
#                                            operator (fracture-tolerating lens
#                                            over any substrate)
#   @glue          @glue(A, B)              `shards/glue.mirror` (Mara P5,
#                                            2026-07-01, 43.5KB); the morphism-
#                                            category correspondence carrier
#                                            (Mesland spectral-triple morphism
#                                            operator)
#   @sre           @sre(@code/X)            per Reed research prose citing SRE
#                                            operator pattern (not landed as
#                                            standalone family-root file; the
#                                            operator pattern is corpus-attested
#                                            through `@code/*` × `@sre`
#                                            composition citations)
#
# `@liquid` joins this altitude as the refinement-lens operator:
# `@liquid(@X)` produces a substrate view where every @X carrier
# admits a refinement_predicate (defined at @epistemologic/liquid
# theory altitude).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# The word `liquid` was substrate-decl'd across FOUR landed altitudes
# BEFORE this composition-operator family-root. This tick lifts the
# operator IN-BETWEEN the four to name the composition pattern they
# ALREADY share:
#
#   1. `boot/std/mirror/liquid.mirror` (Reed 2026-06-04) — grammar-
#      decl `@mirror/liquid` with `type separator` at :13. The
#      mirror-altitude specialization of what a generalized @liquid
#      operator would be. Carries the `---` seam ownership +
#      infer/project pair AT mirror-file altitude. Under this tick's
#      landing, `@mirror/liquid` IS `@liquid(@mirror)` — the
#      composition-operator specialized to the @mirror substrate.
#
#   2. `docs/math/liquid-types/README.md` (Mara 2026-07-05, 30.3KB)
#      — the load-bearing math foundation. §2 operator `refine`,
#      `extract`, `prove`, `route` at theory altitude. This tick's
#      @liquid operator IS the substrate-decl'd form these math
#      operators presume; theory (@epistemologic/liquid) provides
#      the algebra @liquid composes over.
#
#   3. `docs/specs/liquid-types-for-mirror.md` (Reed 2026-06-04,
#      41.7KB) — research spec grounding SOTA (LiquidHaskell / Flux /
#      F* / Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala) + §5 spectral alternative + §6.2
#      :733-758 grammar shape forward-promise. This tick lands what
#      §6.2 shape draft named at composition altitude.
#
#   4. `shards/epistemologic/liquid_extraction.mirror` → migrated
#      2026-07-17 to `shards/epistemologic/liquid/extraction.mirror`
#      (Mara THIS-tick migration cascade `12cdf0e` per Q-C
#      arbitration) — the operational subspecies extracting
#      refinement predicates from doc claims. Under this tick's
#      landing, extraction is `@liquid(@docblock).extract` — the
#      composition-operator specialized to the @docblock substrate
#      via its extract action.
#
# The composition-operator pattern was thus substrate-decl'd across
# four altitudes without a family-root anchor. This tick lands the
# anchor.
#
# === @liquid(@silicon) — the ratified novel discipline ===
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-17 in-transcript verbatim (per Taut scout §0
# preamble):
#
#   > "Route through @silicon + @epistemologic instead of directly
#   > to mirror. Physical machine execution + knowledge/type
#   > extraction preserves the semantic invariants LLVM erases
#   > (borrow-check, ownership, lifetimes = liquid types recovered
#   > at silicon altitude)."
#
# `@liquid(@silicon)` names the extraction-from-binary discipline
# the Kagi state-of-the-art scan (Taut scout §6.1 Search 5,
# 5 sources) found NO canonical dominant discipline for:
#
#   - LiquidHaskell (Vazou 2014): refinement AT source altitude
#   - Flux (Lehmann 2023): refinement AT source altitude
#   - F*: refinement AT source altitude
#   - CompCert (Leroy): semantic preservation, no refinement
#     recovery
#   - Alive2 (Regehr): translation validation, no refinement
#     recovery
#
# `@liquid(@silicon)` recovers liquid refinements (borrow-check,
# ownership, lifetimes) FROM silicon-observed execution
# properties (@epistemologic/reality/silicon/* carriers), back-
# projecting via `@mirror/liquid.project` to source. Novel per
# Alex 2026-07-17 Q-B arbitration + Reed spec §8 novelty
# enumeration.
#
# This tick DECLARES @liquid; empirical @liquid(@silicon)
# discharge is future arc work (the extraction bilateral between
# @epistemologic/reality/silicon and @silicon/algebra will discharge
# through the reflective evaluator).
#
# === Parametric-lens discipline ===
#
# Per Taut scout §7.2 the substrate ALREADY dogfoods the
# lens-composition pattern this operator declares:
#
#   - `@sre(@code/X)` per corpus references
#   - `@bilateral(@code/A, @code/B)` per `shards/epistemologic/pact/
#     bilateral.mirror` (§"@bilateral generalization" — Alex
#     2026-07-17 verbatim reframe) + polyglot spec §5.2 + the
#     `translation_admissible` bilateral block at bilateral.mirror
#     (sentinel `"translation=preserves-meaning"`, arity 1)
#   - `@bilateral(@silicon/algebra, @fate/algebra)` per bilateral.
#     mirror (§"Connection to @kintsugi/algebra" — reframe binding
#     algebra_metalogue_session between speaker-algebras)
#
# `@liquid(@X)` extends the parametric-lens discipline the substrate
# already dogfoods; zero substrate-authority tension per Taut §7.2.
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at `shards/liquid.mirror` declares `@liquid` at family-
# root altitude per @epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace.
# Sibling family-roots at the same depth (composition altitude):
# @shatter (boot/03-shatter.mirror), @glue (shards/glue.mirror),
